    {
      "id": "claim_52a8ba341fa6434c8a5ebb1aae4d96a3",
      "statement": "Compose start order is enforced via healthchecks: the db service must report healthy (pg_isready) before api starts, and keycloak's dependency on api uses condition service_healthy so keycloak only starts once the API's /health endpoint succeeds; frontend depends on api without a health condition.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://compose.yml#L17-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:480b18d27eb932e08602acdeafaea3b4be566a51add4d50ec74778fb90a75e14:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://compose.yml#L67-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a397046184dd2093899715f8b930e6de3f1bc207d7b7649a9fcf24383f8c68b7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8ab606173b994978b15998da8c79a4ad",
      "statement": "The API healthcheck in compose.yml probes GET http://localhost:8000/health using Python's urllib, and that endpoint (defined in backend/api/main.py) exercises the DB session dependency, so a passing healthcheck implies the database connection and startup schema bootstrap succeeded.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/api/main.py#L60-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2e2372bcab92fce26a43b70173aa9dfaa79c37d49d6c0b98204b887343bce27d:"
