    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6ec59845d33e434ab788d5def57708a4",
      "statement": "Backend configuration is a pydantic-settings Settings model composed of PostgresSettings, KeycloakSettings, SeaweedFSSettings, and WikiSettings, using env_nested_delimiter=\"__\" so environment variables are named <GROUP>__<FIELD> (e.g. POSTGRES__HOST); Postgres and Keycloak fields have no defaults and are required, while SeaweedFS and Wiki fields have working defaults.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/api/config.py#L1-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d1eff2f56141350820fdbe6fb02bb798d4e98c89297b511238b68b0ad5b6cb37:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_490d785f6cac435695ffc239a9e7ea82",
      "statement": "There is no Alembic or other automated migration framework: backend/api/database.py's init_db() creates schema by calling SQLAlchemy's Base.metadata.create_all against the models in api.models, and backend/api/main.py invokes init_db() followed by seed_db() at module import time (before the FastAPI app's lifespan runs), so schema creation and seeding execute synchronously on every API process start.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/api/database.py#L29-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:becfa0c93578bff2308939d6c760e8be727ca4b2d50fa60aa9a75e2632b36411:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/api/main.py#L14-L61",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d579c728bdbb0ee46579fb57f70def19e281f3585e96230c0792100de55bad57:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f4b5d928f826478ba3bd7e5fa194daa1",
      "statement": "seed_db() in backend/api/seed.py populates default reference catalogs (CourseBlock, CourseTarget, CourseSubject, CourseRequirement, CourseEqfLevel, CourseType, NeuroPrinciple, CrossSubject, BloomLevel, KrauuCompetence) and SystemSetting rows only when each respective table is empty, so edits to the seed data or SYSTEM_SETTINGS list have no effect on an already-seeded database.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/api/seed.py#L478-L526",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d28c1503f74ed4c7cdeda0ac24fb8ba41b2b08cffcd308b0f6509498895c887e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_712f9ecf5f154a59ac86dcc8a50193a9",
      "statement": "backend/scripts/update_system_settings.py is the operational tool for propagating SYSTEM_SETTINGS changes (from api.seed) into an already-seeded database: for each key it inserts a missing SystemSetting or overwrites only the changed name/model/prompt/description fields of the existing active row, and it is invoked via `make update-settings [KEYS=...]` which runs it inside the running api container, explicitly overwriting any manual edits made through the admin dashboard for the affected keys.",
      "evidence": [
